{%- comment -%}
  Hundred Europe: FAQ under produkterne på udvalgte kollektioner.
  Indholdet vælges ud fra collection.handle. Andre kollektioner viser intet.
  Kilde: 100 Google SEO/tekster/udkast-03-kategorier.md
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign h = collection.handle
  assign show = false
  case h
    when 'badminton-rackets-hndrd', 'power-rackets-nitrix', 'control-rackets-hyfonic', 'speed-rackets-flareon', 'lightweight-rackets-nuclear', 'nuclear-rackets', 'badminton-shoes'
      assign show = true
  endcase
-%}
{%- if show -%}
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Barlow+Condensed:ital,wght@1,800&family=Barlow:wght@400;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  .hg{--ink:#0a0a0b;--soft:#5d584f;--line:#e7e3dc;--gold:#f2a81d;--display:"Barlow Condensed","Arial Narrow",Impact,sans-serif;--body:"Barlow","Helvetica Neue",Arial,sans-serif;font-family:var(--body);color:var(--ink);max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(48px,7vh,88px) clamp(16px,4vw,32px);text-align:center}
  .hg *{box-sizing:border-box}
  .hg-eyebrow{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;font:700 12px/1 var(--body);letter-spacing:.32em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink);margin-bottom:14px}
  .hg-eyebrow::before,.hg-eyebrow::after{content:"";width:24px;height:2px;background:var(--gold)}
  .hg h2{font:italic 800 clamp(30px,3.4vw,44px)/1 var(--display);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0;margin:0 0 28px;color:var(--ink)}
  .hg-faq{border-top:1px solid var(--line);text-align:left}
  .hg-faq details{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
  .hg-faq summary{cursor:pointer;list-style:none;font:600 17px/1.35 var(--body);color:var(--ink);min-height:56px;display:flex;align-items:center;padding:14px 44px 14px 0;position:relative}
  .hg-faq summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
  .hg-faq summary::before,.hg-faq summary::after{content:"";position:absolute;right:6px;top:50%;width:16px;height:2px;background:var(--ink);transition:transform .2s ease,background .2s ease}
  .hg-faq summary::after{transform:rotate(90deg)}
  .hg-faq details[open] summary::after{transform:rotate(0)}
  .hg-faq summary:hover::before,.hg-faq summary:hover::after,.hg-faq details[open] summary::before,.hg-faq details[open] summary::after{background:var(--gold)}
  .hg-faq summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--ink);outline-offset:3px}
  .hg-faq details p{font:400 16px/1.6 var(--body);color:var(--soft);margin:0;padding:0 44px 18px 0}
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.hg-faq summary::before,.hg-faq summary::after{transition:none}}
  @media screen and (max-width:820px){.hg-faq summary{font-size:16px;min-height:52px}.hg-faq details p{font-size:15px;padding-right:0}}
</style>
<div class="hg">
<span class="hg-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow | escape }}</span>
<h2>{{ section.settings.faq_title | escape }}</h2>
{%- case h -%}

{%- when 'badminton-rackets-hndrd' -%}
<div class="hg-faq">
<details><summary>Which Hundred racket is best for beginners?</summary><p>A flexible racket that is easy to play – Nitrix 10 or Thunder if you want power, Hyfonic 1 for all-round play, Flareon 100 for speed, or Nuclear if you want a very light racket.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is a stiff racket better?</summary><p>Not for everyone. A stiff shaft gives the most control to players with good technique, but it is harder to play with. Most players get more out of a flexible or medium shaft.</p></details>
<details><summary>Which weight should I choose – 3U, 4U, 5U, 6U or 7U?</summary><p>4U suits most players. Choose 3U for more weight and power, and 5U, 6U or 7U for a lighter, quicker racket that is easier on your arm and shoulder.</p></details>
<details><summary>Are all colours of a model the same racket?</summary><p>Yes – unless stated otherwise, the colours only differ in design.</p></details>
<details><summary>What is the difference between head-heavy, even balance and head-light?</summary><p>Head-heavy gives more power, head-light gives faster racket handling, and even balance gives you some of both.</p></details>
<details><summary>What string tension should I choose?</summary><p>As a guide: beginners around 18–22 lbs, club players 22–25 lbs and advanced players 24–27 lbs. Never string above the racket's maximum tension.</p></details>
<details><summary>How do I find the right racket?</summary><p>Talk to Kim, our racket advisor. Kim asks about your level and how you play, and recommends a model from the Hundred range.</p></details>
</div>

{%- when 'power-rackets-nitrix' -%}
<div class="hg-faq">
<details><summary>Which Nitrix is easiest to play?</summary><p>Nitrix 10, Thunder and Attack – all flexible and made to help you generate power.</p></details>
<details><summary>Nitrix Pro or Nitrix 70 Venom?</summary><p>Both are top rackets. The Pro is flexible and forgiving; the 70 Venom is stiff and demands more technique.</p></details>
<details><summary>What is the difference between Nitrix 70 Volta and Nitrix Pro?</summary><p>They are very similar. The Volta has a more aerodynamic frame for faster handling but a slightly thicker shaft (7.0 mm vs 6.5 mm), so the two roughly balance out.</p></details>
<details><summary>Not sure which Nitrix to choose?</summary><p>Ask Kim, our racket advisor, for a recommendation based on how you play.</p></details>
</div>

{%- when 'control-rackets-hyfonic' -%}
<div class="hg-faq">
<details><summary>Is Hyfonic good for doubles?</summary><p>Yes – the even balance combines power and fast racket handling, which works for both singles and doubles.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is the Hyfonic 7 stiff?</summary><p>No. It is flexible, which makes it an easy-to-play top racket.</p></details>
<details><summary>Not sure which Hyfonic to choose?</summary><p>Ask Kim, our racket advisor, for a recommendation based on how you play.</p></details>
</div>

{%- when 'speed-rackets-flareon' -%}
<div class="hg-faq">
<details><summary>Is a head-light racket good for doubles?</summary><p>Many doubles players choose head-light for fast grip changes and quick exchanges at the net.</p></details>
<details><summary>Will I lose power with a head-light racket?</summary><p>You get less "free" power than with a head-heavy racket. Choose 3U or 4U for more weight behind the shot.</p></details>
<details><summary>Not sure which Flareon to choose?</summary><p>Ask Kim, our racket advisor, for a recommendation based on how you play.</p></details>
</div>

{%- when 'lightweight-rackets-nuclear', 'nuclear-rackets' -%}
<div class="hg-faq">
<details><summary>Is Nuclear a power series?</summary><p>No. Nuclear is a lightweight series. The rackets are slightly head-heavy, so you can still create some power, but the focus is on low weight and easy handling.</p></details>
<details><summary>What does the number mean?</summary><p>It is the weight in grams: Nuclear 60 weighs 60 g, Nuclear 72 weighs 72 g and Nuclear 78 weighs 78 g.</p></details>
<details><summary>Not sure which Nuclear to choose?</summary><p>Ask Kim, our racket advisor, for a recommendation based on how you play.</p></details>
</div>

{%- when 'badminton-shoes' -%}
<div class="hg-faq">
<details><summary>How should a badminton shoe fit?</summary><p>Snug, so your foot stays in place in lunges and stops – without squeezing your toes.</p></details>
<details><summary>Phenom or Hypercourt?</summary><p>The Phenom is Hundred's top model for intensive training and matches. The Hypercourt focuses on comfort, grip and support.</p></details>
<details><summary>How do I find the right size?</summary><p>Measure your foot and compare it with our size guide – especially if you are between two sizes.</p></details>
</div>
{%- endcase -%}
</div>
